# What this tree refuses to carry, decided here rather than in each clone.
#
# Every entry is a path a command this repository already runs writes into the
# working tree. Without a tracked file the answer comes from whatever each
# contributor's own configuration says, and two contributors then disagree about
# what a checkout contains without either of them doing anything wrong. That is
# the same reason .gitattributes is tracked one file over, for the bytes of a
# fixture rather than for the presence of a directory.
#
# Every entry is anchored to the repository root with a leading slash. A
# directory somebody later names target inside a crate is a different thing, and
# an unanchored pattern would swallow it without anybody deciding to.

# Cargo writes here, for every profile and for the coverage instrumentation.
/target

# The report .github/workflows/coverage.yml writes at the root, which a
# contributor reproducing that measurement locally gets too.
/coverage.json
